<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#piracy">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piracy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as pirates</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piracy is robbery and violence committed at sea. Along the coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> it was a persistent problem, often linked with smuggling and illicit trade. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> conducted campaigns against coastal pirates, known in Chinese sources as wokou, as part of its maritime and defensive policy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piracy.jpg" alt="Piracy" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WarX, edited by Manuel Strehl · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Edward_England.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Eumelus then kept a fleet that cleared the Black Sea of <b>pirates</b> from the Caucasian coast and the Crimean mountains.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bosporan-kingdom">Bosporan Kingdom · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…with Rome, and according to Tacitus, envoys reminded the Senate in 53 CE of the help their city had given to Roman commanders in wars against the Macedonian kings, Antiochus III, Aristonicus, the <b>pirates</b> and Mithridates VI of Pontus; Claudius responded by remitting their tribute for five years.</blockquote><a href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Water Chenla, on the Mekong Delta, had the river's wealth but was more exposed; late in the century it faced war from Javanese <b>pirates</b> who took the delta and then Chenla itself, and it came to depend on the Shailendra dynasty of Java and Srivijaya.</blockquote><a href="/empire/chenla">Chenla · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 3rd century Frankish <b>pirates</b> ravaged the coasts of Gaul and Britain; Carausius was given command of the Channel fleet against Frankish and Saxon raiders around 285, and a famous story tells of Frankish prisoners settled by Probus on the Black Sea who seized ships and sailed…</blockquote><a href="/empire/franks">Franks · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the Middle Ages its ships fought <b>pirates</b> on the North Sea; in 1401 a Hamburg fleet captured leaders of the Victual Brothers, and Klaus Störtebeker and his men were executed in the city.</blockquote><a href="/empire/free-and-hanseatic-city-of-hamburg">Free and Hanseatic City of Hamburg · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>But Red Turban rebels invaded in 1359 and 1361, briefly taking Kaegyong, Japanese <b>pirates</b> ravaged the coasts, and Gongmin was murdered in 1374.</blockquote><a href="/empire/goryeo">Goryeo · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
